# Tiền Đây — Architecture Rules

## General
- Inspect the existing project structure before introducing new files or patterns.
- Prefer the simplest architecture that supports the current product and foreseeable MVP growth.
- Avoid premature abstraction.
- Keep UI, state/business logic, and persistence/data access reasonably separated.

## Source of truth
- `Demo/` is the current V3 UX/UI source of truth.
- When documentation conflicts with `Demo/`, `Demo/` wins until explicitly changed.

## Data model
Current V3 prototype transaction field for how the user paid:
- `account`

This is the documented V3 baseline field. It is not automatically the final production data model.

A V3 transaction object also includes at minimum:
- id
- amount
- category
- detail
- date
- account
- note

Additional fields require a clear product reason. Do not redesign this model in later phases until that phase is approved.

## Persistence
- User-created transaction data must persist using the project's approved persistence layer.
- Do not rely on UI-local mock arrays for production behavior.
- Avoid destructive schema changes.

## State
- Keep a single source of truth for transaction data.
- When a transaction is created, edited, or deleted, dependent screens must update consistently.

## Reuse
- Reuse existing components and utilities before creating duplicates.
- Do not create parallel versions of the same screen/component unless there is a real platform requirement.

## Error handling
- Handle invalid input and persistence failures gracefully.
- Never silently discard user-entered transaction data.

## Technology discipline
- Do not change the app framework, language, build system, or architecture direction unless explicitly approved by the user.
